      "artist": "Richard Avery",
      "description": "A late Victorian stained glass inset in an upper window of Salisbury Museum (the King's House). It shows the coat of arms of Henry Frederick, Prince of Wales (1594-1612), the eldest son and heir apparent of James VI and I, King of England and Scotland, by his wife, Anne of Denmark. Prince Henry died of typhoid fever, in 1612 aged 18. He visited the King's House with his parents in 1610. The inset gives the impression that it was not made for this window. Made by Kempe which dates it as probably late Victorian.",
